# Git workflow (Astrolabe)

## Commit boundaries

- **Finish → commit → next:** When a feature, bugfix, or backlog item is done and builds, commit (or ask the user to commit) **before** starting the next feature or a large unrelated task.
- **One concern per commit:** Do not bundle unrelated features, refactors, drive-by cleanups, or “while I’m here” edits in one commit.
- **Include tracking:** Put `docs/BACKLOG.md` updates in the same commit as the firmware change they describe.

## When to commit

| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Backlog item marked done | Commit, then pick up the next item |
| User asks to implement multiple features | Commit after each completed feature unless they say otherwise |
| Large refactor split across sessions | Offer a checkpoint commit before switching direction |
| Only the user asked for one small fix | One commit for that fix is enough; do not commit unrelated WIP |

## Agent behavior

- **Issue work:** commit, push, open PR to **`integration`**, and merge when CI is green and the scope is a single issue — see [integration-branch.mdc](integration-branch.mdc).
- **Otherwise:** follow the user’s **committing-changes-with-git** rule (commit when they request or clearly authorize).
- At each **feature boundary**, if commits are in scope but not yet requested: briefly say the work is ready to commit and suggest a one-line message — do not start the next feature on top of a large uncommitted pile.
- Do not amend or force-push. Do not push to **`main`**.
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens).

## Commit message style

- One or two sentences focused on **why**, not a file list.
- Match recent repo style (e.g. `Add moon face tap fortune`, `Fix waning moon terminator tint`).

## Branches and PRs

- One **issue** → one **branch** → one **PR** into **`integration`** (see [github-workflow.mdc](github-workflow.mdc)).
- **`main`**: promote only with `./scripts/promote-integration.sh --flash-ok` after hardware flash QA.

